them the one wrf-core revision every consumer resolves; path
dependencies retain their source and provenance trees.
The former private registry trees of grib1_bridge, rw_wps, zarr_bridge
and arwen-ui-vendor have been folded into this shared source. No existing
rustwx crate was overwritten; duplicate copies retain one canonical copy.
Each crate retains its own licence and upstream notice files. Those files
are also reproduced, deduplicated and indexed in the binary-form notices,
because a compiled consumer never sees the vendor tree.

The Zarr inventory remains at
tools/zarr_bridge/vendor-manifest.json. Shared packages are listed in each
applicable product inventory.

The following grant census and missing-text record describe the original
348-directory, 264-name-and-version bridge inventory; the shared-registry
fold does not replace those historical grant declarations. Product
inventories and their reproduced texts remain the current per-build record.

The census contains no GPL, LGPL, AGPL, SSPL, CDDL, EPL or MPL grant.
The single copyleft token anywhere in it is r-efi's disjunctive
"MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later"; WOOF elects MIT and the
copyleft branch is not taken.

Two facts are recorded here because they are gaps rather than
performances, and a notice that omitted them would be worth less:

  * Twenty of the 348 crate directories carry no licence text file.
    Twelve of those directories hold the project's own crates
    (metrust x2, wx-core x2, wx-field x2, wx-math x2, wx-radar x2,
    wrf-core, grib-core), where the only obligation is to ourselves.
    The other eight hold four genuine third-party upstreams, and their
    text is therefore not being reproduced in the vendored tree:
    puffin (Embark Studios, MIT OR Apache-2.0), r-efi (MIT elected from
