Data services (not redistributed)

WOOF downloads or templates requests for data from NOAA (GFS via the
NOMADS filter service and AWS Open Data; HRRR via AWS Open Data), from
the Copernicus Climate Data Store (ERA5; use is subject to the
Copernicus license and requires the user's own account), and relies on
the user-staged NCAR WPS geographical dataset (WPS_GEOG) for static
fields. None of these datasets are redistributed by this repository;
their terms are between the user and the provider.

`woof fetch-geog` downloads WPS_GEOG by default from NCAR's own server
(`--source hf` takes a byte-for-byte mirror of the same tarballs). The
default set carries only permissively licensed sources; these carry
terms of their own:

  * soilgrids.tar.bz2 (the default soil categories, texture_top and
    texture_bot, and the Noah-MP soil archive) is derived from
    SoilGrids250m by ISRIC -- World Soil Information (Hengl T. et al.
    2017, "SoilGrids250m: Global gridded soil information based on
    machine learning", PLOS ONE 12(2): e0169748), licensed CC BY 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/); NCAR generated the
    WPS tiles and the mirror does not modify them.
  * soiltemp_era5_1deg (the default deep-soil temperature) is built on
    the user's machine from the ERA5 1990-2019 hourly climatology
    published by WeatherBench 2 (Rasp et al. 2024, doi:10.1029/
    2023MS004019) under the Licence to Use Copernicus Products. Credit:
    Contains modified Copernicus Climate Change Service information
    (ERA5, Hersbach et al. 2020, doi:10.1002/qj.3803). Neither the
    European Commission nor ECMWF is responsible for any use of this
    information.

Held out of the default set and fetched from NCAR only when named:

  * soiltype_top_30s and soiltype_bot_30s use the FAO-UNESCO Digital Soil
    Map of the World outside the United States (STATSGO, USDA public
    domain, inside it). Its notes (Version 3.6, Jan 2003,
    https://swat.tamu.edu/media/116411/notes.txt) say "(C) FAO/UNESCO,
    1995 All rights reserved worldwide" and "The user shall not reproduce
    for the benefit of third parties the data"; not permissive.
  * soiltemp_1deg is ISLSCP-I's 1987-88 ECMWF annual-mean temperature;
    the ISLSCP-I Vol. 4 record at CEDA states Permitted Use "Unstated" and
    NCAR states none; licence unclear.

With `[static.highres]` enabled, WOOF downloads high-resolution static
sources into the user's own cache_root; none is redistributed here and
each run's receipt carries its source's attribution. The default land
cover carries terms of its own:

  * CGLC-MODIS-LCZ, the 100 m global land cover WRF and WPS ship from
    version 4.5:
    Demuzere M., He C., Martilli A. and Zonato A. (2023),
    doi:10.5281/zenodo.7670653, licensed CC BY 4.0
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). It is built from the
    Copernicus Global Land Service LC100 v3 (Buchhorn et al. 2020) and
    the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere et al. 2022, Earth Syst.
    Sci. Data 14, 3835). WOOF fetches the published GeoTIFF whole from
    Zenodo, unmodified, and maps its classes into WRF's MODIS categories
    at preparation time.


