the trigonometric functions through transcriptions of the library's own
routines rather than through CUDA's. No code under the GNU Lesser General
Public License is transcribed: every routine below comes from a source that
carries a permissive notice, in the library's own copy as well as upstream.

  - woof/hex/native_powf.py adapts Arm optimized-routines v21.02
    (math/powf.c, powf_log2_data.c, exp2f_data.c), Copyright (c) 2017-2019
    Arm Limited, under the MIT licence in LICENSE.arm-powf and
    licenses/LICENSE-Arm-optimized-routines-MIT.txt.

  - The CUDA physics sources compile together with shared device maths
    headers. In this release the physics ports read those headers from the
    regional engine in this same distribution at run time, and the first
    part of this file carries their notices. When this distribution's physics-resources
    builder assembles them from sources inside this distribution, those
    sources sit in woof/hex/data/mpasphys-maths/ (the glibc_flt32,
    glibc_flt64, glibc_trig_flt32 and thompson_aerosol_libm headers, the
    CORE-MATH log10f block, and CORE-MATH log10f, tanhf and erff), with
    their own notices beside them (LICENSE.core-math and
    LICENSE-third-party.txt in that directory). The same notices apply
    and are reproduced in licenses/: Arm optimized-routines logf, expf,
    exp2f, powf, sinf, cosf, and the binary64 exp, log and pow (MIT,
    LICENSE-Arm-optimized-routines-MIT.txt); CORE-MATH correctly rounded
    functions (MIT, LICENSE-CORE-MATH-MIT.txt); and the FDLIBM log10
    reduction (Sun notice, LICENSE-FDLIBM-SunPro.txt).

  - woof/hex/rkind_libm.py includes the qualified WSM6 composition
    of those same shared headers and complex operators. Their original
    notices are retained in the returned source; the licence files named
    above also apply to this composition.

  - log10. The binary32 log10f the MPAS Thompson port evaluates is
    CORE-MATH's correctly rounded log10f (src/binary32/log10/log10f.c,
    revision bc385c2; Copyright (c) 2022-2023 Alexei Sibidanov; MIT). The
    GNU C library 2.43 carries the same routine as
    sysdeps/ieee754/flt-32/e_log10f.c, with the same MIT notice, and
